# gate-proofs.allow -- preflight slugs with neither a test suite naming their
# script nor a mutations.json entry, plus mutation ids that break the
# <slug>.<kebab> convention. Baseline frozen 2026-09-03, not yet reviewed: 15 of
# 33 slugs. The list only ratchets DOWN -- a NEW unproven slug or a NEW
# off-convention id fails gate-registry, and a line that has gained a proof (or
# been renamed) is STALE and must be deleted. The cheapest proof per slug is
# sketched in docs/code-quality-tooling.md.
android-parity
arg-consistency
copy-coverage
critical-fixes
doc-dupes
dockerfile-lint
mirror-consistency
patch-integrity
pkg-names
runtime-paths
sbom
secret-scan
stdout-returns
version-snapshot
workflow-lint
